The parked PIPE dummy-PHY enable in src/pd_atc_pipe_bootstrap.c follows
m1n1 src/usb.c at121fcbf35d4501814b58ca5347926a4173b6a512 (MIT,
Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors), followed by the held-reset/clamp
state from Linux atc.c. The MIT permission and warranty notice above applies.
The native adapter never releases an uninitialized DWC3 core here.

The separate experimental AON normalization accepts only the observed cold
word0x30 or the effective public m1n1 whole-word initialization + Linux
held-reset/clamp word0x10. It does not establish bit5's meaning or general
control semantics. Native callers require fresh physical ACIO-off and
completed DWC3 drain/park proof before this one cold write; no reset release.
